# Spotify RAG V2 Enhancement

## Objective

Enhance the existing Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) pipeline by improving
the data ingestion process, chunking strategy, embedding model, vector database,
and retrieval mechanism while keeping compatibility with the existing Spotify
Global Music Intelligence Platform.

---

## Existing Implementation

- Gold Layer stored in Amazon S3
- PostgreSQL + pgvector
- all-MiniLM-L6-v2 embeddings
- Fixed yearly chunking
- Ollama LLM
- Django chatbot

---

## Proposed Enhancements

### Data Loader

- Incremental loading
- Batch processing
- Validation checks
- Better logging

### Chunking

- Parent-child chunk hierarchy
- Metadata-aware chunk generation
- Deterministic chunk IDs

### Embeddings

- Replace MiniLM with BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5

### Vector Database

- Replace pgvector with Qdrant Cloud

### Retrieval

- Metadata filtering
- Hybrid semantic retrieval

### Generation

- Qwen (planned)
- Existing Django integration

